export anchor DocumentWorkspaceStyle:
    number: 15
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Document workspace
    idea: The dashboard as one calm document page, with a narrow column, a big title, callouts, toggles and properties, beside a slim grey list of pages.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #ffffff, the document
        sidebar: #f6f5f2, the page list and the search field
        hover: #ecebe7, the current and hovered page in the sidebar
        text: #2a2a28, body text, titles and the progress fill
        muted: #6b6a66, property names, column names and meta text
        line: #e9e8e4, row rules, dividers and progress tracks
        linkBlue: #2f5fa7, the primary button, the focus ring, links in callouts and this week's bars
        callout: #fbf3e4 with a #ead9b5 border, the overdue callout
        onTrack: #25613a text on #e6f1e8, the On track tag
        atRisk: #8a5300 text on #fbeed5, the At risk tag
        behind: #a32b1f text on #fbe4e1, the Behind tag and the overdue count
        neutralTag: #4d5c70 text on #eef2f7, team tags
        lastWeek: #8f8d86, last week's chart bars
    type:
        System sans, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI,
        system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Sizes are
        40px bold for the page title, 24px bold for headings, 20px
        semibold for toggle titles, 28px semibold for summary figures,
        16px body at 1.6 line height, 14px for properties, tables and the
        sidebar, and 13px for tags.
    layout:
        A light grey sidebar 240px wide lists the workspace name and the
        pages with a glyph before each, and two project pages nest under
        Projects. A slim top bar holds the breadcrumb Brightwork / Home on
        the left and the search, the notifications bell, the New project
        button and a round initials avatar on the right. The document is a
        centred column at most 760px wide with a 64px line glyph, the big
        title Home, then property rows for Signed in, Date and Needs
        attention, a divider, a greeting sentence, a warm callout for the
        overdue tasks, a This week heading over four figures split by thin
        lines, and three open toggles for Projects, Tasks completed and
        Recent activity. Projects is a database table with Name, Team,
        Status, Progress, Tasks and Due columns and a faint New project
        row under it. Activity is a plain bullet list. Below 860px the
        sidebar becomes a wrapped row of page links above the page, and
        below 560px the figures form a two by two grid and the table
        scrolls inside its toggle.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 48px above the title, 32px above headings, 16px callout padding and 8px table cell padding.
    density: Calm. One narrow column with generous line height, and toggles fold detail away.
    corners: 4px on tags, buttons, fields, callouts and sidebar rows. Avatars are round.
    borders: 1px #e9e8e4 row rules and dividers only, plus the callout border. There are no cards.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        16px thin line glyphs with a 1.6 stroke and round caps sit before
        every page in the sidebar, every property name and every column
        name, and a 64px glyph of the same kind sits above the page title.
        Toggles use a small chevron that turns down when open. Status tags
        carry a circle tick for On track, a triangle for At risk and a
        crossed square for Behind.
    focus: A 2px #2f5fa7 outline offset 2px with 4px rounding. A focused field gets a #2f5fa7 border and a 1px ring of the same colour.
    tone: Plain, personal sentence case, such as Needs attention, Recent activity and Open overdue tasks.
